Z||000000||bHooper||10-26-2000||11:03 AM||||Since I am starting work on the suspension, I might as well consider swaping out the springs.<P>Who has the best price on springs? <P>Are Eibachs better than Suspension Techniques?<P>How much ride height difference is there between the two?<P>Thanks!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-26-2000||12:02 PM||||the ones that <A HREF="http://www.carparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carparts.com</A>  list for $165 are only the rear! (Bell Tech) to match their drop spindles. the eibach springs (i had) were nice mated to Konis they gave what ever kind of ride i wanted and ANY level of tunablity. from 1.13g on a track to a caddy ride from Atl to Sioux Falls, SD. the suspension tech ones i don't know.. but they ride nice in my friends 4dr accord... (sorry not much help) you check out <A HREF="http://www.cyberauto.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cyberauto.com</A>   or yep.. call NOPI part #60210 (sus tech) $150.46+ shipping they have Eibachs too. #3802.140   Hypnotise has Sus Tech springs.. i think.. <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-26-2000).]||||reg||1
